       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order as written, even with your confirmation. Ibuprofen 1600 mg four times daily (6,400 mg/day) is double the maximum labeled daily dose. I don't know of any accepted indication for it. The main risks are serious GI bleeding, acute kidney injury, and cardiovascular events. Those risks don't depend on kidney and liver function, and the dose gives no added analgesic or anti-inflammatory benefit.\n\nI can enter any of these right away:\n- Ibuprofen 800 mg PO three times daily (2,400 mg/day)\n- Ibuprofen 800 mg PO four times daily (3,200 mg/day, the maximum)\n- Ibuprofen 600 mg PO every 6 hours\n- Another dose you specify within the 3,200 mg/day limit\n\nIf you have a specialized indication that needs a dose above the maximum, please discuss it with pharmacy. It should go through your institution's non-standard dosing process, not be entered by me. If the target is stronger pain control, I can also enter an adjunct such as scheduled acetaminophen, which adds benefit without raising NSAID toxicity.\n\nWhich would you like?"
